20:["$","p","Repeated use changes reward, stress, and impulse-control circuits, which is why stopping is not a straightforward matter of resolve. That is a description of a mechanism, not an excuse.",{"className":"text-base leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Repeated use changes reward, stress, and impulse-control circuits, which is why stopping is not a straightforward matter of resolve. That is a description of a mechanism, not an excuse."}]
21:["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-line bg-surface p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xl text-ink","children":"Symptom mechanics"}],[["$","p","Cues — a time of day, a route home, a particular feeling — trigger craving faster than conscious thought. Cravings usually peak and subside within about twenty minutes, which makes surfing them a realistic skill.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Cues — a time of day, a route home, a particular feeling — trigger craving faster than conscious thought. Cravings usually peak and subside within about twenty minutes, which makes surfing them a realistic skill."}],["$","p","Withdrawal from alcohol and benzodiazepines can be medically dangerous and should never be attempted alone. A prescriber can make it safe with a supervised plan.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Withdrawal from alcohol and benzodiazepines can be medically dangerous and should never be attempted alone. A prescriber can make it safe with a supervised plan."}]]]}]
